1. **Implement strict URL scheme validation on the server-side:**
```python
from urllib.parse import urlparse

ALLOWED_SCHEMES = {'http', 'https'}

@app.route('/add', methods=['GET', 'POST'])
def add():
    url = request.form.get('url', '')
    try:
        parsed = urlparse(url)
        if parsed.scheme not in ALLOWED_SCHEMES:
            return render_template('add.html', error='Only http and https URLs are allowed')
    except:
        return render_template('add.html', error='Invalid URL format')
```

2. **Use the |urlencode filter in Jinja2 templates for URL attributes:**
```html
<a href="{{ item.url | urlencode(safe='/:?&=') }}" target="_blank">{{ item.url }}</a>
```

